[00:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[Singing] AI hybrid filmmaking combines&nbsp; real human performance with AI-generated environments&nbsp; to create cinematic stories more efficiently. We are committed to developing&nbsp; a human-first AI hybrid methodology, one that helps creators train&nbsp; the next generation of media professionals and position Singapore as a leader&nbsp;'

[01:03] [scene:interview]
VISUAL: Boi Kwong explains AI's role across production stages.
AUDIO: 'in AI hybrid filmmaking. AI supports every stage of production,&nbsp; from script development to previsualization, production, post-production, visual effects,&nbsp; and even final outputting. Usually, on a production set,&nbsp;'

[01:20] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: Split screen showing actors on a set and the AI-generated environment.
AUDIO: 'we need to spend a lot of time building the set,&nbsp; waiting for the construction, the materials, and erecting the set.&nbsp; Using AI hybrid, you basically create,&nbsp; from the production designer\'s point of view or the director\'s point of view,&nbsp;'

[01:34] [scene:interview]
VISUAL: Samad Jaffar, Production Designer, talks about AI's creative freedom, with a monitor displaying various kitchen environments.
AUDIO: 'exactly what we want. So we actually give more creative control&nbsp; to the filmmakers themselves, and they actually create the world&nbsp; rather than adapt to the world that was given to them.&nbsp;'

[01:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In the beginning, I was a bit worried because I\'m not used to doing it with AI.&nbsp; But after being in it, I\'m beginning to love it&nbsp;'

[01:58] [scene:interview]
VISUAL: A crew member discusses working with a gray background and applying environment details.
AUDIO: 'because there\'s no limit. I can do whatever I want,&nbsp; design whatever I want, down to the details,&nbsp; where previously, budget and everything would restrict me.&nbsp; It was mentioned that there\'s not going to be a whole set.&nbsp;'

[02:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'We\'re working with a gray background. You look at the set,&nbsp; you look at the environment, the ambiance, and then you apply it&nbsp; in terms of the colors, the mood. Whereas this one is kind of reversed.&nbsp; You have to know exactly what, and then you work backwards.&nbsp;'

[02:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then you have to think whether this look will match.&nbsp; Usually, we had to buy the clothes and let the actors try them on.&nbsp; So the advantage of this AI is we can actually test&nbsp;'

[02:45] [scene:interview]
VISUAL: Sng Ye Xiang, Chief Creative & Product Officer / Cinematographer at BYKAI, explains cost savings from not needing physical recces.
AUDIO: 'before even buying the clothes. So we save a lot on costs&nbsp; and have less waste.&nbsp; So in the traditional way, we used to have recces, go on site,&nbsp;'

[02:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and discuss a lot of things. But with hybrid,&nbsp;&nbsp; it\'s a different workflow. We don\'t have to go on site.&nbsp; We just have to decide which location, which mood we need.&nbsp;'

[03:09] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: Crew watching a screen showing an AI-generated scene.
AUDIO: 'With the help of references and stuff, we can actually generate the image.&nbsp; So we save a lot on costs for the art direction and the props.&nbsp; The first thought I have in my mind is: How do I work with this AI world&nbsp;'

[03:49] [scene:result]
VISUAL: Final AI-enhanced scene.
AUDIO: 'and the actual world? So with my practical experience,&nbsp; I feel that discussion with the DP is still a must.&nbsp; Eventually, we can discuss even more, like, can we enhance something&nbsp; from here in the world? Then I recreate it on the set itself.&nbsp;'

[04:02] [scene:result]
VISUAL: Final AI-enhanced scene.
AUDIO: 'Because of this pipeline, we are able to shoot 24 locations&nbsp;'

[04:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in just 8 days.&nbsp; We are not here to fight the technology. AI tools will continue to evolve.&nbsp; So the future won\'t be won by a single tool, but by the one with the best AI hybrid workflow.&nbsp; At BYKAI, AI hybrid is not about replacing filmmakers or performances.&nbsp;'

[04:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It\'s about using AI strategically within a real production workflow.&nbsp; Working with technology such as Beeble allows us to explore masking,&nbsp; background replacement, environment transformations, and relighting,&nbsp;'

[05:10] [scene:interview]
VISUAL: A crew member working on a laptop, discussing AI's role in achieving creative vision.
AUDIO: 'while preserving the original performance and photography.&nbsp; The important thing for us is control: deciding what stays real,&nbsp; what can be transformed, and how AI can help us achieve&nbsp;'

[05:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the final creative vision. What\'s really exciting&nbsp; about working with BYKAI is that they\'re approaching AI&nbsp; from the perspective of filmmakers and real production.&nbsp; Our collaboration has involved not only providing technology,&nbsp;'

[05:36] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Detailed view of Beeble SwitchX UI, showing a node-based workflow for video generation, including text prompts, model (Stable Diffusion 2.0), resolution, and a viewer.
AUDIO: 'but also working closely with their team, looking at actual real-world problems&nbsp; and finding how to fit Beeble\'s technology into their AI hybrid workflow.&nbsp; BYKAI brings strong filmmaking and production experience,&nbsp;'

[05:49] [scene:interview]
VISUAL: A Beeble representative discusses the collaboration with BYKAI.
AUDIO: 'while Beeble brings our research and technology.&nbsp; By working together, we can explore new ways&nbsp; of giving filmmakers greater flexibility and creative control,&nbsp; while preserving the human performance at the center of the work.&nbsp;'

[06:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'We see this as a very positive collaboration, and we\'re excited to continue exploring&nbsp; what\'s possible together. I believe Singapore has an opportunity&nbsp; to lead the region in AI hybrid filmmaking. By combining our creative talent&nbsp;'

